#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198020 :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2 ,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n![](images/d7/d7b8d89cae048a9cd5e04299bebdcb3a5d5d21ac6d5a31c48482aa00ca71517c.svg)\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,x-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=1} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050188 :topic/math-academy-id 3178 :topic/title "Flux in Three-Dimensional Vector Fields"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050508 :topic/math-academy-id 3386 :topic/title "Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94132937-eda0-5e90-a5ac-7f0f9def7aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194136} {:answer/id #uuid "f7544775-c055-5b3c-895a-3510daf49d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194137} {:answer/id #uuid "45e9bfa2-b5ab-5fb6-8215-c0e7746dd7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194138} {:answer/id #uuid "47bb57ce-704e-5663-89a6-934af702d9e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194139} {:answer/id #uuid "608267cb-3d68-525c-bb1c-ef2ceab4fd7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94132937-eda0-5e90-a5ac-7f0f9def7aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194136} :answer-field/id #uuid "977eb979-4b50-5a03-b91d-aa19a8c0611f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6a0f062-0f76-50a3-a357-dfc6f1a08d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-160839" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\,2y,\\,1⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨uv,\\,u+v,\\,1-v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}au{v}^{2}+b{v}^{2}+cuv-u+v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ v & 1 & 0 \\\\ u & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}v & 0 \\\\ u & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & 1 \\\\ u & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,v,v-u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨xz,\\,2y,\\,1⟩{|}_{x=uv\\,y=u+v\\,z=1-v} \\\\  & =⟨uv\\cdot (1-v),\\,2(u+v),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨uv-u{v}^{2},\\,2u+2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨uv-u{v}^{2},\\,2u+2v,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩ \\\\  & =(uv-u{v}^{2})\\cdot (-1)+(2u+2v)\\cdot v+1\\cdot (v-u) \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}-uv+2uv+2{v}^{2}+v-u \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}+2{v}^{2}+uv-u+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot u{v}^{2}+2\\cdot {v}^{2}+1\\cdot uv-u+v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+1=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194750cf-4b33-5153-97c1-bd1b0f21c3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275713} {:answer/id #uuid "30772c46-8461-5daa-94aa-ff5b8a754f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275909} {:answer/id #uuid "45100deb-1ec8-5bbb-b0b4-3c26c5616332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u{v}^{3}+4{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276086} {:answer/id #uuid "45e6001c-4deb-5a8c-b01f-01531e4489d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u{v}^{3}+2{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276094} {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81d9840-6037-5557-81d1-599235b0ea5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} {:answer/id #uuid "40392ee9-b3f1-5009-bd69-fc1a719298c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}v+u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276036} {:answer/id #uuid "66d47ff6-4d2f-51dd-a0bd-fe3a8ddbdd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{u}^{3}v-2u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276396} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d10ecc-5a2a-5169-bb03-eaafe2a1f99a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277369} {:answer/id #uuid "da347498-a4dc-5e22-9cb1-7985c24efdcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c299fe-08c9-5f88-b42b-ca47c7784874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278018}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99addda-c910-54da-a8cb-ae3a5ce916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161249" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,-uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-uv\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+(-2uv)\\cdot (-4uv)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+8{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4065be-6410-5ccf-b764-e323b3954972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275595} {:answer/id #uuid "996e1145-cf3a-5420-96fd-aafd97d1eb20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276855} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e32ea5-a6f3-52a4-b8ec-13ac55fa6f7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277004} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf319d-2d9f-52cc-bda0-79efe3637268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799dfb7-bba2-57d2-9a73-5392e0c83466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278129}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2d1066e-0b79-5532-9ae3-4e710fbc5bc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161303" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}+2v,\\,{u}^{3}+3v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}+bu+c\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩{|}_{x=u+v\\,y={u}^{2}+2v\\,z={u}^{3}+3v} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (6u-6{u}^{2})+0\\cdot (3{u}^{2}-3)+2\\cdot (2-2u) \\\\  & =6u-6{u}^{2}+4-4u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{2}+2u+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6)\\cdot {u}^{2}+2\\cdot u+4\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+2+4=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd609ae-e864-57b8-94a4-273742d368ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275735} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccb8e67-96de-5752-b3c3-d11e0af4993a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275881} {:answer/id #uuid "54d35ae5-86bd-5395-8972-05d0d8d00e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} {:answer/id #uuid "af78fb93-58e2-566e-a85b-fc76c0f645fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277047} {:answer/id #uuid "f88b3e2e-dffa-5fc2-9b42-e62568668267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54d35ae5-86bd-5395-8972-05d0d8d00e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a58223-7188-508a-9949-c05e00640b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ba2bc0a-f01f-56b1-8fa8-5c3da0d50d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161306" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u{e}^{v},\\,u{e}^{-v},\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{e}^{v}+b{e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{-v},\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v},\\,-u{e}^{-v},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u{e}^{v}\\,y=u{e}^{-v}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩ \\\\  & =(u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{-v}+(u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{v}+u\\cdot (-2u) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{e}^{-v}+{u}^{2}+{e}^{v}-2{u}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{v}-{e}^{-v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot {e}^{v}+(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1-1=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1c9dba-209f-56b2-8f1b-b1d0237d58ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275746} {:answer/id #uuid "26a5678b-7a2d-5817-8c83-9403924b91f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275827} {:answer/id #uuid "aff51ef5-48b1-5e4e-9bc6-f47b5b3b48de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}+uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277052} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d084df-38e6-570e-8bc2-f410786a2b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277104} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198} :answer-field/id #uuid "1900b165-70c5-5f9d-ad38-9a5a829338e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277771}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92e0422d-8551-525d-a92c-4ab1ea25fb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-161384" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d89472a-c8a6-58ee-ad06-702bb85242bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398509} {:answer/id #uuid "6ceed292-fdb3-5c81-a5ef-e21d4577bafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398510} {:answer/id #uuid "2e773ddf-4b3c-5bc1-b538-c1702b36529f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398511} {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b5545b-f437-5265-821f-6ea217aea603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} :answer-field/id #uuid "f48bed04-e645-581d-90b2-d43b8caed324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50f21d4c-115f-5f6b-a6fe-50fa77f7169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161251" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)+3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)+{u}^{2}\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡v+{sin}^{2}⁡v)+{u}^{3} \\\\  & =-5{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,-5{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f13cf51-1f17-54c3-b3d0-3a4ed9f6cc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398536} {:answer/id #uuid "0823e1c6-a66c-59c3-bb60-2b11710017b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398537} {:answer/id #uuid "7a803047-69b8-53fa-8d05-7893832957a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398538} {:answer/id #uuid "3330207b-8637-52ec-b488-bd1a488b22dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}+uv+2{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398539} {:answer/id #uuid "915a87fb-c1cd-571b-be39-7c31f1761641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "915a87fb-c1cd-571b-be39-7c31f1761641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398540} :answer-field/id #uuid "af2f16f5-115b-5596-b71d-8a4dab14117a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398535}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd17085b-48fe-5be2-bc57-b62ce4e45b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161383" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,uv,\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y=uv\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =uv\\cdot v+uv\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot u \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189bee50-4a99-5b40-af14-d79a6be4cf78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421767} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab31c93-1b65-5e8b-a761-9f8a56bd7091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421768} {:answer/id #uuid "936a7baa-180a-5ac4-87b7-254a0a451cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421773} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1d5f42-e69e-5804-8ffc-1ba7c0a90d40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421774} {:answer/id #uuid "a21a5496-3418-514f-ae65-4dd4f8f20907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab31c93-1b65-5e8b-a761-9f8a56bd7091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421768} :answer-field/id #uuid "44498254-f6d6-5947-a33a-02e052e8e1fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27b29e44-b12e-5311-b5aa-28b3cb92f7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161304" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,xy,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2v \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2v \\\\ 1 & 2u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,xy,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=2uv} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,2uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,2uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-2v)+uv\\cdot (-2u)+2uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}v+2uv \\\\  & =2uv-4{u}^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\cdot uv+(-4)\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2-4=-2.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198379 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198021 :question/id #uuid "2a32501f-d0f2-5e59-b7cc-a6b459269f6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12357" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x, y, z) = \\left\\langle -y, \\: x, \\: z+2 \\right\\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x^2+y^2$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z = g(x,y)$ for $(x,y) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left( -P\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} - Q\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial y} + R \\right) \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $\\mathbf F(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨-y,\\,x,\\,z+2⟩{|}_{z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨{{-y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-y,\\,x,\\,z+2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(-y)\\cdot (2x)-(x)\\cdot (2y)+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2xy-2xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+2y]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e4ed7d-32e1-561d-a22f-6872ac0c11d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276093} {:answer/id #uuid "79d3f9e1-b09d-5da0-9956-625389bb5691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276584} {:answer/id #uuid "7fce5fdb-d2d4-56fd-b48c-ac35d9caf62f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276636} {:answer/id #uuid "dba9155e-47c3-5323-95b0-44b98e26ea32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277400} {:answer/id #uuid "eed29fd5-8470-5433-bc50-626d03bc72f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45e4ed7d-32e1-561d-a22f-6872ac0c11d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276093} :answer-field/id #uuid "826fd7b3-ffdf-520e-95fa-e603158a44c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277954}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd29749c-bfb5-5726-8ec7-04f9f714fe37" :question/math-academy-id "q-160888" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{z=x-y} \\\\  & =⟨(x-y)+y,\\,2y+(x-y),\\,xy⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(x)\\cdot 1-(x+y)\\cdot (-1)+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-x+x+y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2x+{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(2(1)+{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06423401-c4cb-59a0-9bd6-7e1a82b5b0ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275534} {:answer/id #uuid "0ce5551e-7454-5d22-ae6a-ac13e583b0e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275587} {:answer/id #uuid "1481a58c-6133-58f7-a21d-cabc8d7625ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275668} {:answer/id #uuid "7671f819-6d07-506b-b49f-13d0ef633588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276546} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab9fbd0-cdfd-51f8-ab82-86979d2a493d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1481a58c-6133-58f7-a21d-cabc8d7625ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275668} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed331e7d-c8f9-522c-8244-24e655efebee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278141}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56a2b4c8-31ce-51dd-93f5-6f1083f199f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161553" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x-y)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩{|}_{z=-x-y} \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{e}^{y}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1-x-y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({e}^{x})\\cdot (-1)-({e}^{y})\\cdot (-1)+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{e}^{x}y+{e}^{y}+y-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+e+1-x-\\frac{1}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-x-\\frac{1}{2}+e)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{x}{2}+ex]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+e-1 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1522d126-bc34-5af8-9b6a-e28d9a69cc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275676} {:answer/id #uuid "18a12e63-447a-54f3-aa1b-7655d054b2a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275705} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0d9dd7-0a4c-53a0-93f3-266c540e5806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276630} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ec1fd9-ea87-51b3-9aac-bec86160b60b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277443} {:answer/id #uuid "eb954333-7f24-5dd3-958d-038c55f1b656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb954333-7f24-5dd3-958d-038c55f1b656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b5f25c-b535-59ae-8da4-9392f8bb667d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278131}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "154ea74b-7c8a-5b64-880d-29244a657638" :question/math-academy-id "q-161382" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+y)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\  & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xy(2x+y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{-x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{-y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy(2x+y)}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(-x)\\cdot 2-(-y)\\cdot (1)+xy(2x+y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}+{x}^{2}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{x}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f73d79-8055-5bca-ad98-afa9fe1eca21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275639} {:answer/id #uuid "2489ad8d-d47c-5d5d-acf8-3774325d7221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275804} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4a22ca-44c7-5916-87eb-4e511e7bfbd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8e-1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275885} {:answer/id #uuid "e441be55-99f3-5307-823b-61fbeb9c2f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277470} {:answer/id #uuid "edd11e5f-f65e-5f0e-a5f8-5cb3f2bfbc56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{2}+1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2489ad8d-d47c-5d5d-acf8-3774325d7221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275804} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80fe3bf-3f3b-576e-826d-db2fe76a6dda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278050}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5fb8cb6-33d1-582b-8cf3-53ceebac82e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161435" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le x.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩{|}_{z=x+y} \\\\  & =⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{x+y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{xy}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{e}^{x+y}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(xy)\\cdot 1-(x+y)\\cdot 1+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-xy-x-y+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-xy-x-y+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{x+y}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{2x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{2x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}-{e}^{x}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-e)-(0+\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278522 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f8ea45-7189-5de7-b023-513085bc87a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275684} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8d5990-f27c-5d2a-8556-ade0d064ae64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275747} {:answer/id #uuid "9b81db63-fffe-50ae-abb4-769c30bdcdcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276871} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7a2355-821a-5abf-ae21-cfb859e97e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277145} {:answer/id #uuid "e9752611-528c-5fdc-8927-863cf9474421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d8d5990-f27c-5d2a-8556-ade0d064ae64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275747} :answer-field/id #uuid "6db629ff-d6ea-571f-9225-53d34e230d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277919}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da0b12bf-561c-5907-8348-62e84bca5b63" :question/math-academy-id "q-161481" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ for $-\\pi \\le x\\le 0$ and $-x\\le y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩{|}_{z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)} \\\\  & =⟨{{1}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨1,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y))-0\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y))+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=-x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =0-(-0+(-\\pi )-\\frac{(-\\pi )^{3}}{6}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b71688e-a084-50b0-8ee6-cfbf6ebd32af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e-{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275872} {:answer/id #uuid "4431028f-ab75-5b42-a52f-32fd75e489e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276079} {:answer/id #uuid "745d7976-0dbc-50a2-9490-bc45b40b9a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5e+2{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276530} {:answer/id #uuid "89b5e633-6fda-572c-a63c-6a89752bac4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7e-{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276721} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b62c25-f5f9-5ac7-a005-6cbd37efb361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3e+{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4431028f-ab75-5b42-a52f-32fd75e489e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276079} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b538e17-dfb5-54b8-b49d-76ddb3c1edcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d858f67e-e87d-5922-848f-1cf10db83bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161536" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x}} \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot ({e}^{x})-(x+{e}^{x})\\cdot 0+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}{e}^{x}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{x}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55b0b9b9-6c61-52a0-883d-72dabb5dc5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276237} {:answer/id #uuid "70f28e28-c030-5053-a069-7bc3877eb33b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276493} {:answer/id #uuid "80ad5cf6-f9ff-56a1-bcb6-20cadcc92134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276642} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8eb565-31a6-5155-8e44-4a4d6a7de0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277276} {:answer/id #uuid "fce9c2cc-cb68-5fd2-aff3-f988333f015d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55b0b9b9-6c61-52a0-883d-72dabb5dc5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276237} :answer-field/id #uuid "5439730e-b587-501e-b283-51c217f9d9d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277869}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d38df384-c529-5d23-b152-2f8b3a09208a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161539" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $-x\\le y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy))=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy))=\\frac{x}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩{|}_{z=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(xy)} \\\\  & =⟨{{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(xy),\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({cos}^{2}⁡(xy))\\cdot (\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)})-({cos}^{2}⁡(xy))\\cdot (\\frac{x}{{cos}^{2}⁡(xy)})+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{0}(-y-x+1)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-xy+y]}_{y=-x}^{y=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-{x}^{2}+x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ee01a9e-4d6e-5878-adf2-060b8c43af0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276023} {:answer/id #uuid "868095d1-9b6f-50d0-a2e4-14ea341f041e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276684} {:answer/id #uuid "be04cd4e-9167-5e17-85e8-8eda77bf9d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277171} {:answer/id #uuid "ea250f8f-2bf8-51ef-a17f-c4811c95105a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277523} {:answer/id #uuid "f818f75a-e762-544b-8f16-1c1ee72458c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea250f8f-2bf8-51ef-a17f-c4811c95105a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277523} :answer-field/id #uuid "5926af28-c362-5c51-8ef9-27b5b281cdda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277884}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1788e522-3caf-5313-8725-17c2fd98bec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161541" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2\\sqrt{xy}$ for $3\\le x\\le 4$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩{|}_{z=2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =⟨{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{4xy+1}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}}-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{[-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2x{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+8x+0-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16be5565-2c3b-5f69-b524-980e1e2bf3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275687} {:answer/id #uuid "17111300-baf7-5ae1-b074-f80c3453c930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275692} {:answer/id #uuid "32cd6ba9-9960-5d19-8ac0-24c02b4d1256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275928} {:answer/id #uuid "d089aab2-9fb8-5519-be05-cd9b1526a968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277322} {:answer/id #uuid "da5ba4ac-a3ff-57ea-8b84-e611e12b0b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da5ba4ac-a3ff-57ea-8b84-e611e12b0b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277393} :answer-field/id #uuid "e911db97-27c7-54f3-ad45-0562d2a959a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278136}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "caf172ee-9d85-5048-a736-0f63395a41ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-161542" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩{|}_{z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{y-x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,y-x,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(x+y)\\cdot (2x)-(y-x)\\cdot (2y)+1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2{x}^{2}-2xy-2{y}^{2}+2xy+1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[y-{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(1-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3})-(-1+{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3})]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(2-2{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(2-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})-(-2+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a2c4b7e-5a81-5de2-94d6-7167bf955b26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276431} {:answer/id #uuid "858fcbe8-2cf5-5ca9-990f-91adfe85964d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276674} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2313fb-5b8b-58b3-a0a5-5f823fb6971d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277015} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f28b55-e6f6-5262-ba0f-bd065f0baf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277069} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ac136e-0642-5dac-b405-2d869dca7fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a2c4b7e-5a81-5de2-94d6-7167bf955b26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276431} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7fe5238-ca86-56aa-9732-ac63987785d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0720c99-cc1f-5800-96bf-793fcc7002e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161552" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+y)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2xz⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\ F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2y(2x+y),\\,2x(y+2x+y)⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\  & =⟨{{3{x}^{3}y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{4xy+2{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{4xy+4{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(3{x}^{3}y)\\cdot (2)-(4xy+2{y}^{2})\\cdot (1)+4xy+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6{x}^{3}y-2{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6{x}^{3}y-2{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[-3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}y]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-3{x}^{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-12-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35f2e086-31b9-544a-9b9a-99a08a27f04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373974} {:answer/id #uuid "291af077-cf81-5322-8799-9c4d0a56816f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373975} {:answer/id #uuid "84fcb1f0-4936-5fbf-afb7-a71a059f4960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373976} {:answer/id #uuid "c8544813-339e-5ed8-a745-c0b3a602e975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373977} {:answer/id #uuid "c730413b-a101-500a-a942-8a345613f8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "291af077-cf81-5322-8799-9c4d0a56816f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373975} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d45f19-fa05-53a9-92e1-77a6078e07fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373973}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a86f1df-9194-5ee6-ac19-2bfbeca02663" :question/math-academy-id "q-161447" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,z+2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=y-2x$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2x)=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,z+2x⟩{|}_{z=y-2x} \\\\  & =⟨y,\\,x+(y-2x),\\,y-2x+2x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{y-x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,z+2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot (-2)-(y-x)\\cdot (1)+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2y-y+x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2y+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y+x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{y}^{2}+xy]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(1+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2+2-1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401261 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aab621f-8cde-5ff7-83da-d05fc13356ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-\\frac{17}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401263} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1077bb-f87e-5cca-9aef-16e4fb33aef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+e-\\frac{19}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401264} {:answer/id #uuid "2adea1b0-35c6-5e84-940d-c02c34a5479d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{19}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401265} {:answer/id #uuid "6170ad11-316c-53bb-b473-67e1f8f56f3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401266} {:answer/id #uuid "cccdc272-4ba4-53bf-8e7e-06633eea609a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-e-\\frac{13}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2adea1b0-35c6-5e84-940d-c02c34a5479d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{19}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401265} :answer-field/id #uuid "67d473e4-fb62-570e-a504-252ea46fe0d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401262}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "682d2ef7-9cff-5a52-921d-70cd49bbb080" :question/math-academy-id "q-161476" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x-y}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le x.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}{e}^{x-y}={e}^{x-y} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}{e}^{x-y}=-{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x-y}} \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{-(x-y)},\\,xy{e}^{-(x-y)},\\,{e}^{x-y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{y-x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{xy{e}^{y-x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{e}^{x-y}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨\\frac{1}{z},\\,\\frac{xy}{z},\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-{e}^{y-x}\\cdot {e}^{x-y}-(xy{e}^{y-x})\\cdot (-{e}^{x-y})+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+xy+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-1+xy+{e}^{x-y})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-y+\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}-{e}^{x-y}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-1+{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-x+{e}^{x}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{8}-1+e)-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{8}+e\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Over a Surface"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198022 :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩|}_{x=1+2u+v\\,y=u+v\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (-2)+(1+2u+v)\\cdot 3+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+2v+3+6u+3v+u+v \\\\  & =5u+6v+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[5uv+3{v}^{2}+3v]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5u+6)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}+6u]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10+12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0183618f-3362-5caf-80a5-a35db56f915e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275488} {:answer/id #uuid "0e6cd527-baf3-578b-b158-575236e38ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275598} {:answer/id #uuid "12c49c9b-d152-58b2-80d7-d4d05c4ba56d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275647} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5a323e-80aa-5ee5-8b05-f4d65a56b56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276320} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a62071-81ac-50dc-be9e-62be7ce3c24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a62071-81ac-50dc-be9e-62be7ce3c24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277652} :answer-field/id #uuid "180f5e20-4b61-50e3-abd0-cd720a92e5b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277769}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69fe42a1-24c6-5f53-90f3-883e2fa5e193" :question/math-academy-id "q-160845" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-1,\\,2v,\\,2-3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩|}_{x=u-1\\,y=2v\\,z=2-3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3(u-1)+(2v)+(2-3u-2v),\\,\\frac{2v}{2}-2,\\,-3(u-1)-(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6+(v-2)\\cdot 2+(2v+1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6+2v-4+4v+2 \\\\  & =6v-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[u]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [3{v}^{2}-8v]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11be498b-977a-5f13-82a0-b8754dc5bd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275636} {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} {:answer/id #uuid "bc028827-be53-5841-a899-754876ec3402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277150} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0b90a-2bd6-5552-afc1-f83bdcf172c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277350} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4662bc-b4e4-5fee-98bc-64e89c915aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} :answer-field/id #uuid "42073408-3ed9-5a4e-b4da-76268342b625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6b5a3a2-513f-5721-bf54-260cfc8a8f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160886" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-1,\\,uv,\\,3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩|}_{x=2u-1\\,y=uv\\,z=3v} \\\\  & =⟨2(2u-1),\\,\\frac{(2u-1)(3v)}{3}-2uv,\\,2(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\cdot ⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =(4u-2)\\cdot 3v+(-v)\\cdot (-6)+6v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =12uv-6v+6v+12uv \\\\  & =24uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}24uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}[12{u}^{2}v]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}12v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[6{v}^{2}]_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =6({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb1ebbc-1b66-59c6-bc4c-36473d96ba4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} {:answer/id #uuid "85d8c729-3067-5308-8ef9-00bf4d3de7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276678} {:answer/id #uuid "89edd3d9-c58a-5b81-ba4b-f7481df906e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276723} {:answer/id #uuid "a74d2bae-d261-5258-af7b-a10ec79ffeaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276985} {:answer/id #uuid "dc49e905-67e7-5a8f-9ad4-5d61bb70fa97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb1ebbc-1b66-59c6-bc4c-36473d96ba4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} :answer-field/id #uuid "8068e66d-fe19-5730-b61d-8b3c05169a3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277949}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24885575-8fa2-5424-9a08-3593cc23273c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161260" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(2+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+(u-v+{v}^{2})\\cdot (-2v)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{u}^{2}v+2u{v}^{2}-2u{v}^{3}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-v+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44b20462-99c7-5dec-bd31-d1e7bfd2d3e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276083} {:answer/id #uuid "47ec0a42-a449-5ef7-9620-57343f2509fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276115} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3c185d-7cc5-59b9-a34a-f883b39b5057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276862} {:answer/id #uuid "bb763c3b-1014-5b4d-aa64-f7778d6ff1dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277143} {:answer/id #uuid "ec28bfe5-83c3-5b4b-bd6b-4c685f49f886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec28bfe5-83c3-5b4b-bd6b-4c685f49f886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277548} :answer-field/id #uuid "8345f144-9030-5837-991d-e3b6514dd5e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277957}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "627dbfaa-1fc7-5620-9101-9c85744bbe99" :question/math-academy-id "q-161262" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3u{v}^{2},\\,u-v,\\,2⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩|}_{x=3u{v}^{2}\\,y=u-v\\,z=2} \\\\  & =⟨{(3u{v}^{2})}^{2},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =9{u}^{2}{v}^{4}\\cdot 0+(3u{v}^{2}+u-v)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-6uv-3{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[u{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(u+\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}u]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6(-2+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23825e40-ec53-5f67-9638-35d121d51307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275793} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} {:answer/id #uuid "98e6e4b9-4435-58e2-9d7a-b732cdd0ce08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276849} {:answer/id #uuid "d47ba56f-6b65-598d-b6f5-90728d0382b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277348} {:answer/id #uuid "ebed3c1d-caab-55c6-88ae-97fc928a3dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c0bba0-07fc-5c71-ba73-fcc312a83f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5de597f-04b0-56f5-aa9e-d79ce26e7706" :question/math-academy-id "q-161263" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-v)+uv\\cdot (-2{u}^{2})+v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-3uv-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4}v+{u}^{2}v]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[-3{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4087a83f-b6d4-59eb-ad43-5778e62db807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276039} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf11252-5492-5171-bafa-fea2eb4849ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0daa63-b87d-58b0-ad93-81d0749be7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276857} {:answer/id #uuid "bb812a7c-457e-5b53-bb9a-157b69c0ee22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277146} {:answer/id #uuid "dc487f46-d4f7-596b-b4d5-ade4f4727666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf11252-5492-5171-bafa-fea2eb4849ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} :answer-field/id #uuid "09628fb2-5798-5e67-a99b-89a6c4a88382" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277743}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75e371a5-e04a-5fb9-938c-f538e06e2f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-161273" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,v-u,\\,-2uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2v \\\\ 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-2uv} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\cdot ⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (2u+2v)+0\\cdot (2u+2v)+(v-u)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}-u{v}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{3}v-\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355bef10-0b8c-5536-a445-f01d12172fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275953} {:answer/id #uuid "59ce5885-1e3d-5f19-ba38-dbb31ab5b6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276282} {:answer/id #uuid "638c8aa6-4abb-5caf-80fe-7e02a183ce5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276379} {:answer/id #uuid "821420d2-3a8a-52ab-bf19-2fe3c2fc1b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276652} {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268} :answer-field/id #uuid "c470c898-ccdc-5a03-914c-a796d495fee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278070}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f5f7b83-0f5c-511f-9e98-a4ae85732cc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161278" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨-(u+v)-(-v),\\,u+v-(v-u),\\,-(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-u)\\cdot 1+2u\\cdot 1+v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-u+2u+2v \\\\  & =u+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[uv+{v}^{2}]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(u+1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+u]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0294c002-bd57-57d3-80b3-7fabcd4c0abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275500} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1b7943-d74f-593a-a73d-4f7b2984e272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275563} {:answer/id #uuid "1db67973-261d-5c72-9a22-797cdd70f57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275749} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3d9f2b-1400-51de-a847-0f9dbed86615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276476} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4f51d4-c721-5278-ac9c-1a3d3fac3e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db67973-261d-5c72-9a22-797cdd70f57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275749} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7c1739-5bdb-5824-990f-022e95db8fc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277772}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4391484-a70c-5d5d-8147-34baf59f21fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161283" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u{v}^{2},\\,-1,\\,1-2u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2uv,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {v}^{2} & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩|}_{x=u{v}^{2}\\,y=-1\\,z=1-2u} \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,-3(u{v}^{2})(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(1-2u)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-4uv)+3u{v}^{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-8uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v\\, \\\\  & =-8\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a219dca-1e12-574f-9fc3-d709a89775ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421769} {:answer/id #uuid "4b502ee2-042d-5a3e-86ae-ba6ad14e00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} {:answer/id #uuid "5be10e6b-2fc0-5157-8d4c-a6365644fb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421771} {:answer/id #uuid "ac272ec2-a123-566b-9ae4-94a591001c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421776} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4a967e-d128-5262-a38b-86976eb912e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b502ee2-042d-5a3e-86ae-ba6ad14e00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} :answer-field/id #uuid "de26f158-7713-5413-99c7-ec6ea96881bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421782}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c963e37-fb2b-5cec-bc6e-5cbde0fb10aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-161258" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3uv,\\,u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩|}_{x=3uv\\,y=u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨3(3uv),\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩ \\\\  & =9uv\\cdot (-1)+(-{u}^{2})\\cdot 3v+2\\cdot (-3u) \\\\  & =-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{9}{2}{u}^{2}v-{u}^{3}v-3{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{11}{2}v-3)\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{11}{4}{v}^{2}-3v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}-3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{23}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} {:answer/id #uuid "176992fe-e63a-5f75-8661-ee649edc6971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421766} {:answer/id #uuid "794b5eb2-d0f5-57bd-8363-4337b7e59452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421772} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9f4e2e-e860-55d7-8d5c-c33be0190db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421778} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fec48c-2c4b-5a3b-8559-e99202ca21e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8009739-528a-5b9d-8b7a-977eb7894c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3288098-3c26-556d-b6c9-f206da47adfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-162593" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩|}_{x=-v\\,y=-u\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,-2(-v),\\,-(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot 0+2v\\cdot (-2u)+u\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4uv-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4uv+u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{u}^{2}v+\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2v+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{[{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198031 :question/id #uuid "c69a0f41-5b8f-5fcd-b058-94df2d7984bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-12383" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left\\langle z+2y, \\: 3y+z, \\: x -z\\right\\rangle$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-3x+2y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n![](images/c6/c682f99e66e12fb124beaee9ae090978444e402b74ce675f0eb2f7939c1ed06d.svg)\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u,\\: v,\\: -3u+2v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=-3u+2v} \\\\  & =⟨(-3u+2v)+2v,\\,3v+(-3u+2v),\\,u-(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-3u+4v)\\cdot (3)+(-3u+5v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+12v+6u-10v+4u-2v \\\\  & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}u\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${\\color{blue}u}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/math-academy-id 4145 :topic/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea6d00-8d2b-5733-8616-9267687fd149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423087} {:answer/id #uuid "63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423095} {:answer/id #uuid "84b21f44-ef97-5299-8654-bb5534b15960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423098} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8fdbef-d72d-513a-8e44-4a96d82e4382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}v-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423108} {:answer/id #uuid "e83e93b0-2e8f-5324-b1ed-23d683ac8523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423095} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab05865-9935-59ef-90a4-5cba4fa4f3d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "412e405b-c9a9-5a1c-8e85-45f26189dce3" :question/math-academy-id "q-160887" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v-v,\\,2v-(u+v),\\,uv⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(v-u)\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u-v+u+uv \\\\  & =uv-v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(uv-v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}uv-v\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9d8774c-14c0-5481-9a1f-1c3acd63867a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194292} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce5f03-88a7-5102-bfd3-b0e4a75a4aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} - v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194293} {:answer/id #uuid "31b2be0c-93a0-5cd7-8143-0596b46129e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + uv + v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194294} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce44ca0-320e-5c90-a723-d02a6010576d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194295} {:answer/id #uuid "7423bf6e-47f3-548e-afbe-feee4e861dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u + v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194296}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5503c223-e87a-5159-abb7-434053fd7b58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f754a120-8886-56d3-b535-398f13b91c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398529} {:answer/id #uuid "d28df103-ae23-5647-a506-1bc60c332868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398530} {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} {:answer/id #uuid "e433762d-59a0-5efb-bef2-7687d8583f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398532} {:answer/id #uuid "3a53a3c7-e2f5-50e9-afd4-d3b986017cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u+v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} :answer-field/id #uuid "185487e5-090f-5815-93b2-dfc0c983e691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398528}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3bcb9d3-050c-5ab9-bd2a-436465223147" :question/math-academy-id "q-161360" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}+2uv+{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} {:answer/id #uuid "397e53f3-63a0-518a-999e-8c3d8631bb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275987} {:answer/id #uuid "897e0260-ef83-5fe5-9ee2-95ed9d4cd1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7u+8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276718} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3f2f9b-ef08-5972-b94d-02717ccd84df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277162} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6d4a87-66ae-58b1-806a-631ade59590d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u-8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} :answer-field/id #uuid "8692e3d1-c9bd-5cca-9274-6af9e13d6963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277965}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf481ef-95d3-5b3f-b324-29ecd57febda" :question/math-academy-id "q-161358" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=3x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 5$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-3\\le v\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-2v)\\cdot (-3)+(-v)\\cdot (2)+2u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+6v-2v+2u \\\\  & =-7u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b5412c-a9ab-5d1e-8d26-9a4c8f27c8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275625} {:answer/id #uuid "16ffd34a-40d1-5df6-87ca-5595406b5509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275691} {:answer/id #uuid "85617ab2-8072-5a8d-9456-259cf0bef230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4v-u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276672} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5a4f92-85cc-5237-ba98-a4e395360811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277305} {:answer/id #uuid "fe69b9d6-2d90-53f7-90a8-f4819b62096e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b5412c-a9ab-5d1e-8d26-9a4c8f27c8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275625} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3b6104-863d-512e-9bea-c3b626c9b6e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "279f5fbf-fc31-5667-8b25-7d1c25dc2d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-161441" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,v-(u-2v),\\,u+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,3v-u,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,3v-u,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(3v-u)\\cdot 2+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u+6v-2u+u+v \\\\  & =-2u+7v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y-z,\\,x+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2u+7v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-2u+7v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} {:answer/id #uuid "023841e2-2821-56a0-955a-89084c15f8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275496} {:answer/id #uuid "4d835b30-d2dd-53ba-9310-a5a2961e3b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276160} {:answer/id #uuid "b4df5cbd-8643-5942-bb9e-8d044eb77815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277092} {:answer/id #uuid "f42daa7a-2c08-5500-aa68-d0405d0dc904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v+u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca208624-88d6-5a85-8572-2dd062347b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278079}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06f1e075-9f39-52f0-b9b8-c179d2533ffc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161462" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,v+2(v-u),\\,2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5477038f-1f6e-56c9-abc2-d2382dd8493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7uv-4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373967} {:answer/id #uuid "938e31d9-0fe9-5c52-a191-c068034a6287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u-24v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373968} {:answer/id #uuid "73e0a3dc-0594-5177-ad29-6281fad0f7ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373969} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd2d79e-1a1c-53cf-b530-bcceff073bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373970} {:answer/id #uuid "1188f498-8136-53fa-a7c5-2ca872f32cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938e31d9-0fe9-5c52-a191-c068034a6287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u-24v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373968} :answer-field/id #uuid "f789f76e-872e-5abd-b18f-ca246f894f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373966}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "acc5680d-481f-574e-9c37-7723114fd2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161381" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-4y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 0$ and $-1\\le y\\le 5.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-4v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,-1\\le v\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-4v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-4v+u,\\,v+2(2u-4v),\\,u-4v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-4v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-7v)\\cdot 4+(u-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6u+8v+16u-28v+u-4v \\\\  & =11u-24v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f202e15-0fbe-50af-9841-523a939ec510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373988} {:answer/id #uuid "176843b4-510b-5e14-95d1-94f7f1d2b76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373989} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb6d1ec-f761-53b6-be0f-80e6cadaee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373990} {:answer/id #uuid "73b04bf4-208b-5a5c-aac6-b4ba092785fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373991} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb5f55b-ba54-5712-9575-db91590f82a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb6d1ec-f761-53b6-be0f-80e6cadaee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373990} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a967ea9-62a2-59e7-9156-ea0fff576b7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373987}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94077de1-f15b-584e-aa54-5f345805312b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161467" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2x-z,\\,y-z,\\,z+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=4x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,4u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x-z,\\,y-z,\\,z+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=4u-v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-(4u-v),\\,v-(4u-v),\\,4u-v+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u+v,\\,-4u+2v,\\,4u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-2u+v,\\,-4u+2v,\\,4u⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2u+v)\\cdot (-4)+(-4u+2v)\\cdot 1+4u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8u-4v+-4u+2v+4u \\\\  & =8u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x-z,\\,y-z,\\,z+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8u-2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(8u-2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82fdd23c-cc42-585e-88f4-5b182b40e621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398516} {:answer/id #uuid "23aa505d-ac0a-5049-b866-d1c5cc38bc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398517} {:answer/id #uuid "e4493f5f-d9a0-53f7-a4c1-2310218fdc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398518} {:answer/id #uuid "8e689bac-8fa3-596f-82fa-c4985e2215d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398519} {:answer/id #uuid "8b17b653-bdb9-591a-a066-41676556f6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b17b653-bdb9-591a-a066-41676556f6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398520} :answer-field/id #uuid "d15555d0-ef8f-523d-8686-3e2c75b76cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eec4b66c-4af6-5b13-942b-337cb7b8732a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161357" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8c22e69-9068-5d72-8593-ce78861036f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398523} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4db3f6-9c97-526b-8cb2-065c8f5de466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398524} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2e8a80-65c9-5d70-9b0e-0e801e7e718d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u+v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398525} {:answer/id #uuid "9f182d4d-0129-52ff-90b2-56e5acb487b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u-v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398526} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e4fd3a-37bb-5bcd-85c6-185c9a1d61c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8c22e69-9068-5d72-8593-ce78861036f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398523} :answer-field/id #uuid "396da9a4-de3b-5bd7-8b5e-dfc780e10bb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5e1155b-c484-5f31-a815-946d2d63d6df" :question/math-academy-id "q-161359" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)v\\cdot (-1)+(u-v)u\\cdot (1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-uv+{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}-uv+uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423086} {:answer/id #uuid "3586c1bc-3061-5093-99ca-95e798991986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423088} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1a3ab5-07e2-55d2-b713-d20c37bdda9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423092} {:answer/id #uuid "6197b42b-5e97-5e6b-a1bb-2951dc50be38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423093} {:answer/id #uuid "cacced8e-053e-5057-89f0-678a72c14a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423086} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbc92cc-19ad-54ee-9d42-9ce995a00f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29805411-7a4c-51f7-893d-a0f3dc3cef10" :question/math-academy-id "q-161377" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-x-y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 2$ and $-2\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,-u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,-2\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=-u-v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\,(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\,(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot (1)+({v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2})\\cdot (1)+(-u-v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2}+(-u-v)^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b89c0b5-bd8b-5088-a053-0db9bc0fd31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423085} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423091} {:answer/id #uuid "62a07ee3-0b12-5f4d-81e0-7183964e0136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423094} {:answer/id #uuid "876d48e1-3fb3-5bc6-88d3-a7e99ab5d29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423100} {:answer/id #uuid "b65ee624-a7db-5060-ba14-007644627aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423091} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce1231b-682c-5119-8b60-1e600b81511c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423118}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92e8ddd2-ccb6-5c20-b74b-2f784e857a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-161379" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-3\\le y\\le 0.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-3\\le v\\le 0\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\,(u-v)^{2},\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\,(u-v)^{2},\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1+(u-v)^{2}\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}5uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "556660a7-ba40-5142-a23c-96cdb3bb38b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-23v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423090} {:answer/id #uuid "86aaa33f-073f-5b9c-b6ed-02e42f1370d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12u-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423099} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa80cac-9ed0-54f2-a0fb-a71697486081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u+14v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423101} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-17v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423103} {:answer/id #uuid "b721d1da-8cb3-5423-bdff-f515271a77db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-17v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423103} :answer-field/id #uuid "de6e4169-2fd0-5a0b-b7fe-172964aca58f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423119}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef91d27f-5ce3-5c48-b5b9-4ec732b3b2e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161471" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+z,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-3y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+z,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-3v} \\\\  & =⟨u+u-3v,\\,2(u-3v),\\,v+u-3v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u-3v,\\,2u-6v,\\,u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2u-3v,\\,2u-6v,\\,u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2u-3v)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-6v)\\cdot (3)+(u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+3v+6u-18v+u-2v \\\\  & =5u-17v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-17v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(5u-17v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral"}]}
